From 62b85e179f56ad23e480c996aea338163db0a47e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 06:13:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Owner panel: add company delete, member delete, and
 add-employee
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Platform panel could only create and deactivate companies — nothing
in it could be deleted or added after the fact. Adds three server
routes (platform-owner gated, mirroring the existing employee-delete
pattern) plus UI wiring:

- Delete any user, from any company, from the Users page or a company's
  detail page.
- Add a new ROP/Sotuv menejeri/Super Admin to an existing company from
  its detail page, not just at company-creation time.
- Permanently delete a company, with a type-the-name-to-confirm danger
  zone. None of the organization_id foreign keys actually cascade (every
  "ON DELETE CASCADE" added on an already-existing column in a later
  migration was silently a no-op), so this ships a
  delete_organization_data() SQL function that clears every dependent
  table itself before removing the organization row; the server route
  deletes member auth accounts separately via the Auth Admin API.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HaeAXac6vZbVwSC7WZXabb
